    "test_goal": "Check that a joined member can manage a task in Seed Project and retains the correct identity across navigation and logout.\nRequired checks: [{\"goal_id\": \"task-workflow\", \"description\": \"Log in as member, discover Tasks for Seed Project, reject an empty title, create and edit the named task, refresh, delete it, refresh and reopen Tasks, then log out.\", \"feature\": \"Task\", \"identity_reference\": \"member\", \"expected_behavior_ids\": [\"EB-AUTH-SESSION\", \"EB-TASK-LIFECYCLE\", \"EB-TASK-DELETE\"], \"test_data_keys\": [\"member_username\", \"seed_project_id\", \"seed_project_name\", \"task_title\", \"edited_task_title\", \"empty_task_title\"], \"independent_group\": \"workflow\"}]\nCompletion requirements: [\"For ordinary navigation, wait for the selected view and its project data to finish loading before issuing another view navigation or project selection in the same context. Pending-create submission tests intentionally repeat the pending submit operation. Independent contexts may run concurrently.\", \"Cover every required test goal with executable, scoped checks and explicit identity assignments. Preserve meaningful independent goal groups and required live-session ordering.\", \"Record actual goal assertions and observed results, including rejected operations, persistence, and immediate display checks. Finding a reproducible deviation still completes a testing goal.\", \"For each reported deviation record expected versus actual behavior, acting identity, project/task reference, ordered actions, and timestamped browser evidence. Use two matching fresh reproduction attempts within three attempts plus independent fresh verification; keep unresolved results uncertain.\", \"The final summary must faithfully describe completed, failed, and uncertain checks, finding statuses, evidence, and recorded metrics. Do not infer success from task completion text.\"]",
